WHAT: Detects alloca instructions whose memory is only written to
(stored but never loaded) and eliminates them as dead.

WHY: Temporary aggregates that are constructed but never read waste
memory allocation and store instructions.

GAS IMPACT: None on rosetta contracts. Fe's allocation patterns use
obj.alloc rather than raw alloca for most temporaries, and the object
load/store pass already handles dead object stores.

TEAM NOTES: This optimization targets a pattern that Fe doesn't generate
for the benchmark contracts. The real dead-store issue is in Fe's std
library [first; N] array initialization, which generates 31 provably
dead obj.stores — a different pattern that requires either Fe source
changes or loop-aware OLS.
